 "title": "Unbounded direct-image comparison",
 "statement": "Let $k$ be a finite or algebraically closed field, let $\\ell$ be a prime invertible in $k$, let $A$ be a finite commutative ring annihilated by a power of $\\ell$, and let $g:X\\to Y$ be a finite-type morphism between finite-type $k$-schemes [def-pc-scheme, def-weil-finite-type-morphism]. Use the unbounded derived categories of ordinary module sheaves over the constant discrete ring $A$ [def-weil-pbc-derived-categories, def-weil-pbc-proetale-modules] and the comparison morphisms $\\nu_X,\\nu_Y$ [def-weil-pbc-site-comparison-morphism]. For every $K\\in D(X_{\\mathrm{ét}},A)$ the canonical comparison\n$\\alpha_K:\\nu_Y^*Rg_{\\mathrm{ét},*}K\\longrightarrow Rg_{\\mathrm{proét},*}\\nu_X^*K$\nis an isomorphism. Here $Rg_*$ is the total right derived direct image, computed on K-injective resolutions [sk-def-sfb-derived-categories], and $\\alpha_K$ is the mate of\n$g_{\\mathrm{proét}}^*\\nu_Y^*Rg_{\\mathrm{ét},*}K\\cong\\nu_X^*g_{\\mathrm{ét}}^*Rg_{\\mathrm{ét},*}K\\to\\nu_X^*K$\nunder the derived inverse-image/direct-image adjunction [sk-def-sfb-derived-categories]. The underived direct images are [def-weil-pbc-direct-image, def-weil-pbc-proetale-operations], and the inverse images are [def-weil-pbc-inverse-image, def-weil-pbc-proetale-operations]. The displayed inverse-image isomorphism is [sk-thm-pe-direct-image-comparison]; the last arrow is the étale derived counit.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-six-functors-basics/sk-prop-pe-unbounded-classical/sk-prop-pe-unbounded-classical-direct-image.md",
  "place": "Statement; canonical mate definition, proof sk-prop-pe-unbounded-classical-direct-image.proof.md"
 },
